abstract: >-
  Recursive Axis Conditioning (RAC) is a loop for generating synthetic corpora.
  It asks the generator to name the axes along which its own outputs vary, ranks
  those axes, conditions on their most different levels, and splits an axis into
  finer ones once it stops producing new items. On coverage of a held-out
  human-written reference, RAC places first of twelve corpora at matched sample
  size (0.4441 against Alpaca's 0.3722), with a corpus a twentieth the size of
  Alpaca's.
